   "html_text": "We generally take arguments built around practical necessity to be responsible to and modulated by the urgency and force of the necessity. The point is easier to see when we consider collective agents, so let us take up Korsgaard’s political analogy once more. A state that aspires to having all activity within its jurisdiction be its own actions is totalitarian. Democratic states sometimes mobilize themselves in a way that approximates this extreme: usually, in times of all-out war. For instance",
